4. PRE/POST-PINCH COUNTS ON THE WARNING FIXTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fixture: 0.1 cm offset seam (offset = 0.1), 3 coplanar quads:
  quad1 (0,0)-(4,0)-(4,4)-(0,4); quad2 (4,0)-(6,0)-(6,4)-(4,4);
  quad3 (4.1,0)-(6,0)-(6,4)-(4.1,4)   [quad3 is quad2 duplicated at x+0.1]

Pipeline numbers (extent=6.0, quant_step=0.0, eps=6e-7, snap_tol=0.003):
  - weld: quads 2&3 share REAL vertices (6,0),(6,4) -> welded to v4,v5;
    seam vertices (4,·) and (4.1,·) stay distinct (0.1 >> eps).
  - snap remap = {} -> the 0.1 seam does NOT snap closed (0.1 > snap_tol).
  - grouping: all 6 triangles in ONE planar group (quads 2&3 connected via
    welded far vertices, quad1 connected to quad2).
  - _boundary_loops residual_out:
      residual_pairs = {{4,5},{4,6},{5,7}}   (net = 2 each)
      pre_pinch_residual_count  = 6   (2 copies each: (4,5)x2,(6,4)x2,(5,7)x2)
      post_pinch_residual_count = 6   (group-level, over the 2 pinch-split loops)
    Why: T-junction splitting (tjunc_tol=snap_tol) splits quad2's seam edges
    at the (4.1,·) fragment vertices, and the duplicated far edge (6,0)-(6,4)
    plus the split sub-edges each survive cancellation 2:0 -> net=2.
  - decompose per-face: the inner loop [6,4,5,7] merges into the outer via
    _merge_loop_into_outer (shared residual edges cancel), leaving the merged
    face loop with 3 residual occurrences -> warning count = 3.
  - result: has_warnings=True, 1 face, area 24.0, warnings
    [{"type": "unpaired_boundary_edges", "count": 3}].

Fixture iteration note: a plain 0.1 gap (NO shared far vertices) produces
TWO separate planar groups / two clean faces with NO residuals - the offset
seam must keep the duplicated fragment connected to the base fragment via
shared (welded) vertices for the edge imbalance to materialise. The chosen
fixture does exactly that and the warning is genuinely exercised (remap={}
proves the seam did not snap).

